// Camp scenes (W3). A node with a 'topic:' header is a camp scene, and the topic is what the DAY
// was - the fights that happened, the Nerve that got spent, whether you ended up on the floor. The
// vocabulary is the engine's: loss, boss, bloodied, trouble, wounded, untouched, quiet.
//
// A night falls back to 'quiet' and to nothing else, because every other topic asserts something
// about a day the companion would then be wrong about. Write a quiet scene.

title: the_quiet_night
speaker: wolf
topic: quiet
---
Nothing tried to eat us today. That is a day. #line:nothing_tried_to_eat_us
Sleep. I will wake you if the water changes. #line:i_will_wake_you
===

title: after_a_bad_one
speaker: wolf
topic: bloodied
---
Sit down. No - all the way down. #line:sit_all_the_way_down
You bled on my map. That is the second time this month. #line:bled_on_my_map
It will keep. Most things keep. #line:most_things_keep
===

title: the_stalk_is_dead
speaker: wolf
topic: boss
---
It is dead. I watched it stop. #line:i_watched_it_stop
I have never smelled anything go quiet like that. #line:go_quiet_like_that
===

title: still_standing
speaker: wolf
topic: untouched
---
Not a mark on you. Do not get used to it. #line:not_a_mark_on_you
===

title: after_the_floor
speaker: wolf
topic: loss
---
You went down. #line:you_went_down
I am not going to say anything else about it tonight. #line:nothing_else_tonight
===
